PLEASE NOTE: ==================================================================
PLEASE NOTE: EDMARK'S ESOTERIC FUN MACHINE — GRAND ENSEMBLE CONDUCTOR
PLEASE NOTE: CANONICAL 1972 INTERCAL SCORE (DON WOODS & JAMES M. LYON)
PLEASE NOTE: ORCHESTRATES DYNAMIC SECTIONAL MASKS, BREATHING, AND CADENCES
PLEASE NOTE: ==================================================================
PLEASE NOTE: THE PULPIT. :1 LEAD, :2 PULSE, :3 BASS, :4 ORGAN, :5 CHIMES,
PLEASE NOTE: :6 CHOIR, :7 FUNGAL, :8 FUN MACHINE. #1 PLAYS AND #0 RESTS.
PLEASE NOTE: .1 <- #N OPENS SECTION N. A SECTION PLAYS THE REGISTERS AS THEY
PLEASE NOTE: STAND WHEN THE NEXT SECTION OPENS. .3 <- #S STARTS THE TURNAROUND
PLEASE NOTE: ON STEP S; FROM THERE TO THE LOOP'S END THE BAND PLAYS THE
PLEASE NOTE: REGISTERS AS THEY STAND AT GIVE UP.

PLEASE NOTE: THE CREATURE WHISPERS ITS ARRANGEMENT WORD .5 AND ITS SHADOW .6
PLEASE NOTE: (EVERY BIT FLIPPED). EACH CHOICE BELOW SELECTS ONE BIT WITH ~, SO
PLEASE NOTE: A PHRASE ALWAYS SUMMONS THE SAME FORM.
PLEASE DO WRITE IN .5
DO WRITE IN .6

PLEASE NOTE: THE FUN MACHINE BELONGS TO THE PLAYER. NO LATER ORDER MAY REST IT.
DO :8 <- #1
PLEASE IGNORE :8

PLEASE NOTE: NO SECTION FALLS BELOW FIVE BAND VOICES, AND PULSE AND BASS HOLD
PLEASE NOTE: THE FLOOR UNTIL THE BREAKDOWN, SO NO FORM SOUNDS THIN.

PLEASE NOTE: I. EXPOSITION GROOVE. LEAD, PULSE, AND BASS SET OUT; ORGAN AND
PLEASE NOTE: CHOIR EACH MAY COLOUR THE OPENING OR STAY IN THE WINGS.
(10) PLEASE DO .1 <- #1
DO :1 <- #1
DO :2 <- #1
DO :3 <- #1
DO :4 <- .5 ~ #2
DO :5 <- #1
DO :6 <- .5 ~ #4
DO :7 <- #1

PLEASE NOTE: II. ANTIPHONAL CONVERSATION. THE CHOIR SINGS OVER PULSE AND BASS,
PLEASE NOTE: AND EITHER THE LEAD OR THE ORGAN ANSWERS IT, NEVER BOTH. THE
PLEASE NOTE: CHIMES MAY BREATHE.
(20) PLEASE DO .1 <- #2
DO :1 <- .5 ~ #8
DO :4 <- .6 ~ #8
DO :5 <- .5 ~ #16
DO :6 <- #1

PLEASE NOTE: III. GRAND TUTTI APOTHEOSIS. EVERY VOICE SOUNDS.
(30) PLEASE DO .1 <- #3
DO :1 <- #1
DO :4 <- #1
DO :5 <- #1

PLEASE NOTE: IV. HYPOGEAL BREAKDOWN. THE PULSE FALLS AWAY; LEAD AND ORGAN CARRY
PLEASE NOTE: THE TUNE OVER EITHER THE BASS OR THE CHOIR. THE CONDUCTOR TRIES TO
PLEASE NOTE: HUSH THE FUN MACHINE TOO, BUT :8 IS IGNORED.
(40) PLEASE DO .1 <- #4
DO :2 <- #0
DO :3 <- .5 ~ #64
DO :6 <- .6 ~ #64
DO :8 <- #0

PLEASE NOTE: THE TURNAROUND STARTS ON STEP 10 OR 11, COUNTING FROM 0: #3 $ .7
PLEASE NOTE: MINGLES BINARY 11 WITH ONE MORE BIT OF THE WORD INTO 10 OR 11.
PLEASE NOTE: COME FROM STEALS CONTROL BEFORE THE LEAD CAN LEAVE; PULSE, BASS,
PLEASE NOTE: AND LEAD COME HOME FOR THE NEXT CYCLE, AND THE CHOIR MAY JOIN THEM.
DO .7 <- .5 ~ #256
(60) DO .3 <- #3 $ .7
DO :1 <- #0
(100) PLEASE COME FROM (60)
DO :1 <- #1
DO :2 <- #1
DO :3 <- #1
DO :6 <- .5 ~ #32
PLEASE GIVE UP
